From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luke Craig <lacraig3@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 19:14:23 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] panda: before_find_fast before each TB lookup

panda_do_flush_tb() (pandare2 flush_tb, enable_precise_pc and friends) and plugin unload only set
flags, which panda_callbacks_before_find_fast acts on; nothing called it, so neither ever happened.
Call it before each TB lookup in cpu_exec_loop, where pandang had it. Without --enable-panda it is
an empty inline.

SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-2.1-or-later
Origin: panda-re/qemu
---
 accel/tcg/cpu-exec.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/accel/tcg/cpu-exec.c b/accel/tcg/cpu-exec.c
index 5ab1284f32c018acca0b4ad82158b2ebfd10f34b..a8bb249ffa903fd6a7def35a1a26ebffe9bc1250 100644
--- a/accel/tcg/cpu-exec.c
+++ b/accel/tcg/cpu-exec.c
@@ -1042,6 +1042,9 @@ cpu_exec_loop(CPUState *cpu, SyncClocks *sc)
                 break;
             }
 
+            /* PANDA: pending plugin unloads and TB flushes (may leave the loop) */
+            panda_callbacks_before_find_fast();
+
             tb = tb_lookup(cpu, s);
             if (tb == NULL) {
                 CPUJumpCache *jc;
